==English==
{{Wikiquote}}

===Etymology===
Arabic {{term|مجاهد|sc=Arab|tr=mujáhid}}, from [[mu-]] ''one who'' + {{term|جاهد|sc=Arab|tr=jāhada||to wage holy war}} = {{term|جهاد|sc=Arab|tr=jihād||holy war as a religious duty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{enPR|mo͝ojäʹhid}}, {{IPA|/mʊˈʤɑːhid/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/mU"dZA:hid/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|mujahideen}}

# {{Islam}} a  Muslim engaging in [[jihad]], especially armed jihad; a [[jihadist]]

